# Where the client reaches the service. Vite fixes this into the bundle at build
# time, so it is a build input rather than a runtime lookup — which is what lets
# the output stay static files with nothing executing on the server to serve it.
#
# The default, used when this is unset, is /api: the same origin as the static
# files. That is the arrangement `DEPLOYMENT.md § Deployment architecture`
# deploys — one reverse proxy serving the client's files and forwarding /api to
# the service — and it is why the client needs no cross-origin request.
#
# No trailing slash. The value must resolve to the service's root.
VITE_API_BASE_URL=/api
